{
  "name": "Log every campaign reply as a Salesforce task",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Log every campaign reply as a Salesforce task\n\n### How it works\nKeep Salesforce complete without copy and paste. Every new or interested reply from an Argorant campaign starts the workflow. It searches Salesforce for a contact with that email. If there is one, the reply is logged as a completed task on that contact. If not, the workflow creates a lead with the name and company from the reply and logs the task there. Out of office replies are left out by Argorant.\n\nNo credits are used.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Activate the trigger with your Argorant credential. Argorant webhooks come with the Pro plan, and your n8n needs a public HTTPS address.\n4. Add a Salesforce credential to the four Salesforce nodes.\n5. Check the lead source value in **Create a lead**.\n\n### Customization\nLog only interested replies by removing the New Reply event, or search leads as well as contacts.",
        "height": 592,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "dacc62d6-d815-4c76-ab92-5221718d78a1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Match in Salesforce\nContacts are matched by email. Unknown people become a lead first.",
